<<^ code="&#x0001;" namespace="⚕" from="?" -> to="lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook">>
```toml meta
cacheable  = true
file-path  = "bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook.mem"
l-space    = "lararium"
mana       = 15
manao      = 15
manaoio    = 14
namespace  = "&#x2695;"
retain     = true
revised-on = "2026-08-09"
role       = "the go-live founding rite, in TWO BRANCHES: a REHEARSAL founding (containers, disposable, repeated until it bores) and a KEEPER founding (the real hearth, once, irreversible) — they share every movement but the clear. The exact CLI sequence that rehearses, clears a vessel fresh-from-void, stands the device + three founding kahu (SELF-STOOD or CONTRACTED, per the True Name Model), forges + custodies the pre-rotation reserve (compromise-resistant Shamir 2-of-3 cards), seals + backs up the vault, regenesizes, goes LIVE, stands a Herm crossroads where a family needs one, and grows the Nexus. Carries the reserve-custody independence rule + the recovery-cost frame + the identity-class split + the founding-mode ⊥ carriage-contract disambiguation, and serves as the OPERATOR-INSTRUCTION SOURCE a reader (human or agent) resolves the next command from. Operator-ruled 2026-07-20; branched + True-Name-aligned 2026-07-27; THIRD PASS 2026-08-06/07 re-points the seat join from the PRIVATE pet-name to the DECLARED HANDLE (three acts per founding command: --name labels privately, --handle declares outward, --seat stands for a chair), gathers the names onto the fleet via `persona sync`, RETIRES the built-in founding names (the roster forms from what stood; the threshold derives majority), re-homes the seal per-operator at <lares>/nexus, and lands the @nexus LIFECYCLE (born by act · lives by ley-line traffic · quiet by absence — no admin capability anywhere; succession rides ROTATE under the standing pre-commitment) plus the bag-HOME axis (repository | hearth | ley, fail-closed to hearth). FOURTH PASS 2026-08-08: ① names what the clear MUST NOT touch (the acquired library and the repo registry survive every founding — the library rebuilds from NOTHING); a founder meets two new surfaces (#/bags-and-shelf) — every bag declares itself (cap-tier ⊥ home, DISK-OWNED so no wiki edit can re-home a bag) and the acquired shelf holds books outside every tracked tree, referenced by collection name rather than path. FIFTH PASS 2026-08-09: the ground CLEARS — deps brought current (build green, 1682 specs + 3318 tests, zero failures), the AI-instruction pointers outside the repo repointed off a dead path generation, ⓪′ preflight gains the playwright-binary leg and reports a WALK, ④ gains the two passphrase env vars with the shell-history hygiene that keeps a seal worth sealing, and ③′ gains the three questions that decide a guardian name plus the ruling that guardians MAY stand unassigned at founding. Carries one RULED rename: `hoʻāla` fails its lexicon check — Māmaka Kaiao already coined it for `to format, initialize, as a computer disk`, the inverse of the preserving waking-floor it named here, and it sat a few lines from the irreversible clear; the concept and its grounding stand and the pet-name falls — it now reads THE WAKING FLOOR, plain English, after `ho'omaka` (spent on `start a computer program`), `kahua` (spent on `database field`) and `paepae` (free, but already carrying that exact metaphor for a Native Hawaiian nonprofit) each failed the same check. WALKED 2026-08-09: every movement stood across two cycles and this meme needed NO amendment, which the rite sets as its own bar — a silent document rather than a green report; four of the five failures that got there were INSTRUMENTS (an impatient wait, a seed carrying another founding's address book, a gate inspecting where it had to connect, a probe that rebuilt what it measured) plus one silent misroute a green suite reported as fine. Also lands the BOOTSTRAP RE-HOME (operator-ruled): the social bootstrap — one vessel's address book — leaves the corpus root for <lares>/vessel, beside the docs it addresses and inside the wipe zone, so it dies with them rather than by a wipe-list naming it; genesis/ carries the baked island ALONE and a seed becomes safe to copy. And the HOME SPLIT (operator-ruled): THREE WORDS, NO SYNONYMS — lares names the SPIRITS, lararium names the HOUSE, lar names the NAMESPACE — and every siting answers WHOSE IS THIS. LARES PASS, THE LARARIUM ABIDES: the acquired library and the sensoriums are the house's and stand at <lararium> (~/.local/share/lararium), while identity, seal, repo registry, hearth bags and the vessel substrate are the spirits' and stand at <lares> (a Lar's keys ARE that Lar), and watermarks alone stand at <state> (delete at will). Back up <lararium> and <lares>; the wipe zone standing STRUCTURAL is the consequence, since a tier held by its own house leaves no list to widen by a path segment."
status     = "rite"
status-why = "the founding rite, in two branches — rehearsal and keeper; WALKED end-to-end 2026-08-09, two cycles, no amendment"
tags       = ["mesh/carry-contract", "api/pono/persona-policy", "mesh/siege-resilience", "mesh/charter-chain"]
type       = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path   = "ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook"
